D = [
    decision("c0021", "needs_evidence", "Azad's hierarchy is established; a post-work mechanism or society-wide suppression of available automation is not.", ["src-player-primary"],
             "The primary briefing describes rank, sex hierarchy and the ban on unnatural assistance during Azad matches. That is relevant political evidence, but the tournament rule is not a general prohibition on AI in production. The Culture's technological superiority also belongs to the visitor's civilization, not automatically to the host economy.\n\nKeep this candidate unresolved until primary passages establish how goods are produced and how ordinary Azadians obtain necessities. A wealthy, cruel empire is not by itself an automation scenario. The word Azad meaning machine or system must not be mistaken for evidence that machines have replaced its workers.",
             "Review the Imperium city tour, career system and any civilian production passages; separate a game-assistance restriction from an economic automation policy."),
    decision("c0022", "needs_evidence", "Affront cruelty and genetic engineering are documented, but its productive and distribution arrangements remain unclear.", ["src-excession-synopsis", "src-banks-civilisations-list"],
             "The consulted material identifies an advanced civilization that mistreats subordinate beings and exploits a stolen Culture fleet. Those details establish neither the extent of routine labor automation nor an entitlement to necessities. Military machinery borrowed from another polity cannot silently supply the missing civilian economy.\n\nBiological engineering could matter if manufactured service populations replace work by the dominant species, but that relationship needs a primary passage and an explicit population scope. Do not turn any unpleasant advanced society into regime three by default. The candidate remains a lead rather than a scored record.",
             "Read Excession's Affront-host scenes for actual service labor, property and subsistence rules."),
    decision("c0023", "needs_evidence", "The candidate combines materially different caste, reform and postwar periods without sufficient economic evidence.", ["src-chelgria-caste"],
             "The caste order changes before the disastrous war, so a single label for all Chelgrian civilization risks combining incompatible snapshots. Repression, reform and wartime loss are not themselves measures of automation or post-work access.\n\nChoose a period only after checking civilian production and the material consequences of caste membership in Look to Windward. The afterlife system may supply another social scenario, but it is not automatically the same as the biological society or proof that living Chelgrians no longer need to work.",
             "Review Ziller's accounts and the pre-reform economy; append a separate afterlife candidate only if its arrangements are sufficiently described."),
    decision("c0024", "needs_evidence", "The official synopsis supports enslavement and elite ownership, not a complete automation-based economy.", ["src-surface-publisher"],
             "Lededje's Intagliated status establishes a coercive personal relationship. It does not show that every citizen's livelihood has been replaced by automated output, nor that all advanced digital systems serve ordinary provision. The novel's simulated Hells are another institution with a distinct population.\n\nA final record needs the actual civilian production and access mechanism of the Sichultian Enablement, with the enslaved and excluded population included in scope. Do not borrow the Culture's guarantees or assign universal destitution from one person's captivity. The title remains in the queue with a precise evidence gap.",
             "Review Veppers's industrial holdings, the meaning of Intagliated labor and ordinary household provisioning in the novel."),
    decision("c0025", "needs_evidence", "GFCF technological level and foreign policy do not establish any of the economic axes.", ["src-banks-civilisations-list"],
             "The reference identifies the GFCF as a named, technologically advanced polity in Surface Detail. That supports identifying the candidate, but provides little civilian economic information. A level-seven label does not prove universal material abundance, broad ownership or a population freed from work.\n\nLeave its admission and coordinates unresolved. The sources presently encountered are far stronger on diplomatic behavior and conflict than on distribution. A distinct name or military capability is not sufficient reason to add another completed Culture-universe point.",
             "Find primary descriptions of the GFCF's economy and AI rights; exclude if the novel supplies no relevant social mechanism."),
    decision("c0026", "included", "A distinct biologically organized post-need society retains vestigial money and military institutions.", gz, society_id="gzilt-before-sublimation"),
    decision("c0027", "needs_evidence", "Morthanveld social transition and constrained AI rights are relevant, but the available reference is internally unreliable and economically incomplete.", ["src-banks-civilisations-list"],
             "The narrative overview describes residual monetary exchange and an approach toward Culture-like arrangements. Its table simultaneously labels the polity as AI-ruled, making mechanical use of the summary unsafe. A quoted primary discussion encountered elsewhere indicates that full AI freedom is precisely one of the changes still at issue.\n\nThis is a promising transition candidate, but a megastructure and peer-level technology do not establish universal provision or effective ownership. Retrieve the actual Matter passage on going Culture before assigning the control axis, and look for further civilian economic detail. Do not resolve a contradiction by selecting whichever line gives an attractive coordinate.",
             "Read the primary Morthanveld discussion in Matter, corroborating money, AI citizenship and material access independently."),
    decision("c0028", "zero_variant", "Religious restriction of true AI supplies the zero-variant connection; welfare and participation remain open.", idi, society_id="idiran-empire-before-defeat"),
    decision("c0029", "duplicate", "No materially distinct distribution/control mechanism has yet been established beyond the Culture economic model already recorded.", ["src-elench-passage"],
             "The quoted Excession passage establishes a separate Culture-derived group with a different aim: changing itself through contact. That is a philosophical and diplomatic difference, not yet a demonstrated change in material guarantees, productive ownership or human–AI authority.\n\nUnder this project's rule against multiplying the same economic model by every faction name, retain the Elench as a related polity in the decision ledger rather than a second completed point. Reopen the decision if a primary passage demonstrates a distinct mechanism along the requested axes. The unrelated EVE corporation statistics are not lore evidence.",
             "Check the complete Excession context for a substantive economic or control difference before creating a separate record.", duplicate_of="culture-main"),
    decision("c0030", "included", "Common goods are an explicit entitlement, but juvenile exclusion prevents an uncomplicated universal-utopia placement.", dw, society_id="algebraist-dwellers"),
    decision("c0031", "zero_variant", "Systematic AI persecution preserves a biologically controlled order despite the demonstrated existence of capable machines.", me, society_id="algebraist-mercatoria"),
    decision("c0032", "needs_evidence", "Cryptosphere uploading and rescue technology do not yet establish the civilian labor and distribution system.", ["src-feersum-setting"],
             "Feersum Endjinn presents digital afterlives, emerging machine ecology and political conflict on a far-future Earth. These are relevant technological ingredients, but the reviewed overview does not establish what ordinary people must do to obtain food, shelter or continued support.\n\nThe physical kingdom and virtual crypt also have different inhabitants and institutions. A combined record could silently attribute the security of one realm to the other. Review the primary passages before deciding whether to split them, retain a zero variant, or exclude the work for insufficient economic description. Familiarity with the author's Culture setting supplies none of the missing facts.",
             "Review living-world provision and crypt maintenance/control separately, using Bascule, Gadfium and Sessine passages.")
]

